  "question": {
    "text": "A coil of self inductance <math><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> and resistance of <math><mn>0.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> is connected through a switch to a battery of internal resistance <math><mtext>&#160;</mtext><mn>0.9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> . After the switch is closed, the time taken for the current to attain <math><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">%</mi></math> of the saturation value is:&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>[</mo> <mrow> <mi>ln</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow> <mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow> </math>",
    "image": null
  },
