  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The instantaneous current in an LR circuit is given by the equation :<br />(instantaneous current)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>&nbsp;are the instantaneous current, saturation current, resistance, time and inductance respectively.</p><p>Given that the current becomes so percent of saturation current.<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0.8</mn></mrow></mfenced><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#937;</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mtext>&#937;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#937;</mtext></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br />Therefore, the time is:<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">ln</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.016</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p>",
